-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Spellbound
  Publisher   Mastertronic Added Dimension, 1985
  Version     1.2

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Spellbound (1985)(Mastertronic Added Dimension)(128K)[Magic
              Knight 2].z80
  MD5         929d9e7ffaeeb9a88a3e03e32cfe9aef

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Magic Knight in silver-grey armour; every character painted
              by its parts: Florin the dwarf with a winged helmet, red tunic
              and brown beard, Thor with red hair and a blue tunic, and the
              rest. A painted set, colourist not named.

  Pace        original (+1.46% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless, v2.09 card,
              against the plain build, input keyed to updates, lockstep
              checked, 2 seeds (+1.34%, +1.46%))

  Changes     1.1: writes the whole alt ROM image (Sinclair's ROM plus the
              hooks), so the ROM's own interrupt code can never run the hooks.
              1.2: the Magic Knight is drawn about three times faster and the
              game's interrupts stay on while sprites update, so it keeps
              closer to the original's pace (+1.4% in JNext); the game keeps
              its own CPU speed after each update; no change to what you see.

  Note        Known issues: none found in testing; pace in JNext +1.3 to +1.5%
              against the original, default and Enhanced alike (+0.5 to +0.7%
              once walking; the first half-second of play up to +26% while the
              Knight's pictures are first made). Missing: the cheats are
              unplayed by a person (only strength and time checked in the
              simulator); not reached in testing: the puzzles, spells that
              succeed, orders to characters and the ending; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite strength
   2  Infinite time
   3  Infinite spell power
   4  Their strength kept
   5  Their spell power kept
   6  Their happiness kept
   7  Their stamina kept

